1
00:00:04,660 --> 00:00:06,700
This is Trigun.

2
00:00:30,680 --> 00:00:32,400
Oh, my God.

3
00:01:39,060 --> 00:01:42,737
Hey, boss, how long are you going to
keep me held up in this place, huh?

4
00:01:42,820 --> 00:01:46,897
He got two of our idiots already while
we sat around twiddling our thumbs.

5
00:01:46,980 --> 00:01:48,757
You should have let me handle it.

6
00:01:48,840 --> 00:01:50,417
That's what you should have done.

7
00:01:50,500 --> 00:01:52,597
All right, then, I'll let you go next.

8
00:01:52,680 --> 00:01:54,357
I'll even set the stage for you.

9
00:01:54,440 --> 00:01:58,205
I expect you to entertain him
with a unique performance of Trix.

10
00:01:58,440 --> 00:02:00,180
You can be reasoned with.

11
00:02:00,360 --> 00:02:02,478
Let's hope the reward is reasonable.

12
00:02:05,640 --> 00:02:08,699
So, are you gonna make him
go at it alone this time?

13
00:02:11,520 --> 00:02:12,350
Hardly.

14
00:02:12,433 --> 00:02:14,137
I'm a firm believer
that an audience always

15
00:02:14,220 --> 00:02:16,697
gets more pleasure from
a drama with a twist.

16
00:02:16,780 --> 00:02:18,200
It's a simple formula.

17
00:02:18,520 --> 00:02:21,932
The greater the tragedy, the
greater the emotional effect.

18
00:02:39,560 --> 00:02:41,020
I'm worried, Meryl.

19
00:02:41,160 --> 00:02:42,925
It's been two whole weeks now.

20
00:02:48,480 --> 00:02:51,480
I'm sorry this is as far
as we can travel together.

21
00:02:52,060 --> 00:02:52,890
Why?

22
00:02:53,200 --> 00:02:55,000
It's your job or your life.

23
00:02:55,800 --> 00:02:57,624
Which is more important to you?

24
00:02:58,900 --> 00:03:00,420
I can't explain now.

25
00:03:01,540 --> 00:03:03,481
If I did, you'd be put in danger.

26
00:03:04,360 --> 00:03:06,301
So it's been a lot of fun, but...

27
00:03:06,640 --> 00:03:08,360
Well, I guess that's all!

28
00:03:11,040 --> 00:03:11,900
Poor Mr.

29
00:03:12,120 --> 00:03:13,885
Vash, I wonder how he's doing.

30
00:03:14,960 --> 00:03:18,517
You know him, he's undoubtedly
goofing around in some town somewhere.

31
00:03:18,600 --> 00:03:20,600
I'm sure he's just fine and dandy.

32
00:03:21,460 --> 00:03:22,480
Wait for me!

33
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:26,059
Hey, did you hear?

34
00:03:26,880 --> 00:03:30,797
Remember the guy in the white suit who
had caused the saloon riot the other day?

35
00:03:30,880 --> 00:03:33,757
Well, he apparently turned
out to be one of Vash's gang.

36
00:03:33,840 --> 00:03:34,670
Oh, yeah.

37
00:03:34,753 --> 00:03:38,834
That would explain a lot, including
why his methods were so dang vicious.

38
00:03:39,160 --> 00:03:40,220
But he took off.

39
00:03:40,640 --> 00:03:41,757
Yeah, that's right.

40
00:03:41,840 --> 00:03:45,137
I guess at this point, we should count
our blessings if we got off so easy.

41
00:03:45,220 --> 00:03:47,161
Yeah, he's a devil in a red coat.

42
00:03:47,260 --> 00:03:48,319
That's what he is.

43
00:03:48,460 --> 00:03:50,578
Damn, I wish he'd just dropped dead.

44
00:03:51,360 --> 00:03:54,057
How can you stand there and say
such awful things about him?

45
00:03:54,140 --> 00:03:54,970
Huh?

46
00:03:55,053 --> 00:03:58,037
I mean, after all, you have no
idea what kind of person he is.

47
00:03:58,120 --> 00:03:59,649
I think you're disgusting.

48
00:03:59,780 --> 00:04:00,610
Huh?

49
00:04:01,120 --> 00:04:02,080
Gee, Meryl.

50
00:04:14,960 --> 00:04:17,257
Walk your own path with
your head held high.

51
00:04:17,340 --> 00:04:18,777
I just have to keep saying it.

52
00:04:18,860 --> 00:04:19,690
Right.

53
00:04:20,320 --> 00:04:21,280
Millie? Yes?

54
00:04:21,520 --> 00:04:22,477
We've got to get going.

55
00:04:22,560 --> 00:04:23,657
We have a lot of work ahead.

56
00:04:23,740 --> 00:04:25,620
Let's stop wasting time. Okay.

57
00:04:26,260 --> 00:04:29,117
If necessary, we'll follow
him to the ends of the Earth.

58
00:04:29,200 --> 00:04:33,259
It's not only our job now, it's
become our mission to track him down.

59
00:04:41,180 --> 00:04:42,768
Hello, chair, how you been?

60
00:04:47,560 --> 00:04:50,560
Legato, I am the one that
is hunting you this time.

61
00:04:50,960 --> 00:04:52,960
I will find you whatever it takes.

62
00:04:56,560 --> 00:04:59,197
That sounds real cool in
my head, but in reality,

63
00:04:59,280 --> 00:05:02,117
I haven't got a clue as to
how I'm going to find him.

64
00:05:02,200 --> 00:05:03,788
Oh man, what am I gonna do?

65
00:05:06,100 --> 00:05:08,477
Not only that, the more time
I have to think about it,

66
00:05:08,560 --> 00:05:13,325
the more frightening it becomes, and now
my knees are starting to knock together.

67
00:05:13,720 --> 00:05:16,191
Oh man, I actually have to fight this guy!

68
00:05:17,320 --> 00:05:20,217
How can I possibly win such a
battle or even have a chance to

69
00:05:20,300 --> 00:05:22,857
survive a fight with the guy
who smiles with those evil eyes?

70
00:05:22,940 --> 00:05:24,617
The answer is I can't.

71
00:05:24,700 --> 00:05:25,537
I'm gonna be slaughtered.

72
00:05:25,620 --> 00:05:26,450
That's all.

73
00:05:26,533 --> 00:05:27,363
It's not even funny.

74
00:05:27,446 --> 00:05:28,697
I should just back out.

75
00:05:28,780 --> 00:05:30,277
That's what I should do, all right?

76
00:05:30,360 --> 00:05:32,560
Yeah, yeah, for once I'm right. Yeah.

77
00:05:32,920 --> 00:05:34,297
You're right about one thing.

78
00:05:34,380 --> 00:05:35,380
You're not funny.

79
00:05:35,520 --> 00:05:37,517
You change your tune
faster than radio station.

80
00:05:37,600 --> 00:05:39,877
Yeah, well, life ought to
be fun after all, right?

81
00:05:39,960 --> 00:05:40,790
No.

82
00:05:42,140 --> 00:05:44,022
Hey, that's super tasty, mister.

83
00:05:44,180 --> 00:05:47,239
I'll have another salmon
sandwich if you don't mind.

84
00:05:54,660 --> 00:05:58,960
Augusta, I'll be waiting for
you at Augusta Fastestampede.

85
00:05:59,260 --> 00:06:01,848
You will acknowledge
my request immediately.

86
00:06:02,320 --> 00:06:06,900
If you do not meet my request, this is
a sample of what will happen. Don't!

87
00:06:11,400 --> 00:06:12,230
Why?

88
00:06:12,313 --> 00:06:13,143
Who did this?

89
00:06:14,920 --> 00:06:16,980
There's no blood. Huh? What?

90
00:06:17,200 --> 00:06:18,177
Do you actually know him?

91
00:06:18,260 --> 00:06:19,613
This guy, you know him?

92
00:06:21,660 --> 00:06:22,960
It must be him.

93
00:06:23,300 --> 00:06:25,653
He's the only one capable of doing this.

94
00:06:26,080 --> 00:06:26,910
Legato.

95
00:06:27,020 --> 00:06:28,020
You called him?

96
00:06:28,420 --> 00:06:29,420
He's your friend?

97
00:06:29,540 --> 00:06:30,717
Hey, is he your friend?

98
00:06:30,800 --> 00:06:34,682
Do you want me there so bad you
would kill the innocent to get me?

99
00:06:34,980 --> 00:06:35,810
All right.

100
00:06:35,940 --> 00:06:37,234
I'll go there, Legato.

101
00:06:37,580 --> 00:06:39,580
I'll face you on your home ground.

102
00:06:40,600 --> 00:06:41,940
Hey, who are you?

103
00:06:42,900 --> 00:06:43,730
Me?

104
00:06:43,813 --> 00:06:44,835
Who the heck are you?

105
00:06:50,420 --> 00:06:51,900
Hey, easy there, pal.

106
00:06:52,100 --> 00:06:53,100
Where's the fire?

107
00:06:54,140 --> 00:06:57,800
Listen, it's Vash the Stampede.
He's here. I'm telling you.

108
00:07:01,660 --> 00:07:02,600
Oh, my gosh.

109
00:07:02,700 --> 00:07:03,817
Are you sure about that?

110
00:07:03,900 --> 00:07:05,817
Yeah, he's running
rampant through Augusta,

111
00:07:05,900 --> 00:07:08,517
blasting away with that
big silver gun of his.

112
00:07:08,600 --> 00:07:09,430
It's true.

113
00:07:09,513 --> 00:07:13,028
That crazy bastard's gonna do
to Augusta what he did to July.

114
00:07:16,040 --> 00:07:18,216
Well, it's a good thing we found him.

115
00:07:18,920 --> 00:07:22,332
Hmm, what in the hell could
that man possibly be thinking?

116
00:07:24,940 --> 00:07:26,780
My name is...

117
00:07:27,340 --> 00:07:29,340
Vash the Stampede!

118
00:07:34,360 --> 00:07:35,595
Ladies and gentlemen,

119
00:07:35,820 --> 00:07:39,417
forgive the lack of warning, but I'm
afraid it's time for my daily massacre!

120
00:07:39,500 --> 00:07:41,397
And if you don't believe
I'm the real thing,

121
00:07:41,480 --> 00:07:43,957
take a long look at me
and start freaking out!

122
00:07:44,040 --> 00:07:45,460
Observe my red coat,

123
00:07:45,680 --> 00:07:49,280
my lovely blonde locks, And
if you're still having doubts,

124
00:07:49,420 --> 00:07:52,538
check out my one hundred
percent accurate gunmanship!

125
00:07:58,620 --> 00:08:00,497
If you people don't want to die today,

126
00:08:00,580 --> 00:08:03,577
get at least a hundred miles away
from this place as fast as you can,

127
00:08:03,660 --> 00:08:05,307
and then happily ever after!

128
00:08:10,260 --> 00:08:12,201
Finally, that's the last of them.

129
00:08:12,360 --> 00:08:14,997
Why couldn't that nihilistic jerk
have picked a better location?

130
00:08:15,080 --> 00:08:18,300
I used up all my energy
just chasing people out.

131
00:08:18,640 --> 00:08:19,700
I'm poofed.

132
00:08:24,100 --> 00:08:25,380
I don't like this.

133
00:08:25,960 --> 00:08:27,820
It reminds me of the last time.

134
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:34,353
Something's not right here unless you...

135
00:08:36,300 --> 00:08:37,130
Blood!

136
00:08:46,520 --> 00:08:48,900
Do you like my decorations?

137
00:08:51,180 --> 00:08:54,360
In this game, losers don't get to go home.

138
00:08:54,800 --> 00:08:55,980
They go to hell.

139
00:08:57,020 --> 00:08:58,079
Did you kill them?

140
00:08:58,980 --> 00:09:00,880
I am the fifth gung-ho gun.

141
00:09:01,340 --> 00:09:02,960
My name is E .G. Mann.

142
00:09:03,280 --> 00:09:04,751
Did you kill them or not?

143
00:09:05,140 --> 00:09:07,375
Damn, you are a noisy one, aren't you?

144
00:09:07,640 --> 00:09:09,287
What if I did, chicken shit?

145
00:09:09,420 --> 00:09:14,361
You don't seem to want to kill anyone, so
someone had to step up and cover your ass.

146
00:09:15,400 --> 00:09:20,157
And besides Blondie, you
have fallen into my court,

147
00:09:20,240 --> 00:09:22,760
gee, aren't you the poetic one?

148
00:09:23,560 --> 00:09:28,517
Are you telling me that I only have
two choices, to die or to let die?

149
00:09:28,600 --> 00:09:31,437
Whoa, cowboy, don't be such a drama queen!

150
00:09:31,520 --> 00:09:34,597
Only one more has to die.

151
00:09:34,680 --> 00:09:36,417
Just stand there like a good boy.

152
00:09:36,500 --> 00:09:39,540
As soon as I take you
down, it'll all be over.

153
00:09:41,160 --> 00:09:41,990
What?

154
00:09:48,900 --> 00:09:50,100
What's going on?

155
00:09:54,440 --> 00:09:57,240
That bastard is trying
to cut in on my action.

156
00:09:58,060 --> 00:10:00,677
If I have chosen to dispatch
my saber at this time,

157
00:10:00,760 --> 00:10:03,557
the situation may have
escalated into a real problem.

158
00:10:03,640 --> 00:10:07,717
You would have at least been knocked
senseless by your humanoid typhoon there.

159
00:10:07,800 --> 00:10:08,630
Sure, right?

160
00:10:08,713 --> 00:10:10,437
Well, now it's getting interesting.

161
00:10:10,520 --> 00:10:11,637
Looks like you're the favorite.

162
00:10:11,720 --> 00:10:12,720
What's your name?

163
00:10:13,240 --> 00:10:14,828
Forgive my lack of manners.

164
00:10:15,800 --> 00:10:17,506
Allow me to introduce myself.

165
00:10:17,720 --> 00:10:20,014
I am the ninth gung-ho gun of Jigenzan.

166
00:10:20,180 --> 00:10:24,004
Trained by the masters of the Ito
school, I am Raidei, the blade.

167
00:10:24,740 --> 00:10:30,080
I hold no personal grudge against you, but
I wish to engage you in Shi 'ai. Shi 'ai?

168
00:10:33,760 --> 00:10:35,140
I can't read that!

169
00:10:38,640 --> 00:10:42,277
If you cannot mean Japanese, then I'll
give you an abbreviated explanation.

170
00:10:42,360 --> 00:10:43,889
It's a fight to the death.

171
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:44,997
What's in it for you?

172
00:10:45,080 --> 00:10:47,817
You playing along with
Legato's little farce as well?

173
00:10:47,900 --> 00:10:50,817
I would happily walk the path
of carnage a thousand times,

174
00:10:50,900 --> 00:10:53,757
and a thousand times again
for the mastery of Bushido.

175
00:10:53,840 --> 00:10:54,670
What?

176
00:10:54,753 --> 00:10:58,817
Because there is something only visible
when you stand before the Deathly Abyss.

177
00:10:58,900 --> 00:11:01,317
I believe you have seen
this too, have you not?

178
00:11:01,400 --> 00:11:03,576
I haven't seen anything there at all.

179
00:11:04,320 --> 00:11:05,560
Except my own fear.

180
00:11:06,280 --> 00:11:07,110
That's too bad.

181
00:11:07,193 --> 00:11:08,577
that I think you should experience.

182
00:11:08,660 --> 00:11:09,490
Hey!

183
00:11:09,573 --> 00:11:10,403
That mental state!

184
00:11:15,900 --> 00:11:17,040
Come on, now.

185
00:11:17,440 --> 00:11:19,980
It's my job to slice and dice this guy.

186
00:11:21,080 --> 00:11:21,910
Ridiculous.

187
00:11:21,993 --> 00:11:25,797
It would appear you simply did not hear
what I told you just a few minutes ago.

188
00:11:25,880 --> 00:11:26,710
You're right.

189
00:11:26,793 --> 00:11:27,623
I didn't.

190
00:11:30,240 --> 00:11:31,260
What? Huh? Huh?

191
00:11:31,400 --> 00:11:33,988
Your match was quite
over before my arrival.

192
00:11:36,560 --> 00:11:37,980
That fast gunmanship.

193
00:11:38,220 --> 00:11:40,396
Words fail to describe its greatness.

194
00:11:42,040 --> 00:11:44,657
That man was never an
opponent to be humbled by you.

195
00:11:44,740 --> 00:11:46,257
You were completely out of your lead.

196
00:11:46,340 --> 00:11:47,399
Your turn is over.

197
00:11:48,880 --> 00:11:53,233
Take heart in the fact that you may
have served to amuse him for a moment.

198
00:11:57,240 --> 00:11:58,200
You... slime.

199
00:11:59,140 --> 00:12:01,120
Yes, let it burn within you.

200
00:12:01,320 --> 00:12:03,260
I feel it build and fester.

201
00:12:03,880 --> 00:12:07,762
Angry aura released through your
every pore, my knees are shaking.

202
00:12:08,960 --> 00:12:11,901
That alone makes my trip
to this place worthwhile.

203
00:12:12,260 --> 00:12:14,700
It is the source of my greatest pleasure.

204
00:12:20,120 --> 00:12:23,540
Come on, I'm in your debt. Ready?

205
00:12:51,100 --> 00:12:52,280
Is that all you got?

206
00:12:52,400 --> 00:12:53,518
Cause me real harm!

207
00:12:53,760 --> 00:12:55,878
Never heard of warrior's compassion?

208
00:12:56,040 --> 00:12:58,700
I can't hit you in any
way if it'd kill you.

209
00:12:59,000 --> 00:12:59,877
Quite the arrogance.

210
00:12:59,960 --> 00:13:00,977
A real eyesore.

211
00:13:01,060 --> 00:13:03,197
It blurs my path to spiritual awareness.

212
00:13:03,280 --> 00:13:06,157
My friend, people don't
change their ways that easily.

213
00:13:06,240 --> 00:13:09,717
You actually think we're People, absurd!

214
00:13:09,800 --> 00:13:15,117
You and I are men, yet not of
we are dark, diabolical puppets.

215
00:13:15,200 --> 00:13:17,437
What we are—our demons.

216
00:13:17,520 --> 00:13:18,350
demons

217
00:13:24,300 --> 00:13:25,680
Wow, what is that?

218
00:13:25,980 --> 00:13:28,980
I don't know, but it's
definitely not a good thing.

219
00:13:29,380 --> 00:13:30,210
You're right.

220
00:13:30,293 --> 00:13:31,317
Do you think it's Vash?

221
00:13:31,400 --> 00:13:32,377
We've got to help him.

222
00:13:32,460 --> 00:13:33,290
Let's go!

223
00:13:33,373 --> 00:13:34,203
Wait, Meryl!

224
00:13:34,720 --> 00:13:35,550
What's wrong?

225
00:13:35,820 --> 00:13:37,460
We can't this time. Mr.

226
00:13:37,580 --> 00:13:39,477
Vash said it's too big for us to handle.

227
00:13:39,560 --> 00:13:41,207
This is seriously dangerous.

228
00:13:41,360 --> 00:13:43,600
I am well aware of the danger, Millie.

229
00:13:44,300 --> 00:13:45,130
Meryl!

230
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:51,657
Why don't you stop wasting time
here and fight me like you mean it?

231
00:13:51,740 --> 00:13:53,120
Ah! Fight me!

232
00:13:56,780 --> 00:13:58,620
Now that was a huge shockwave.

233
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:00,000
Oh, no big deal.

234
00:14:00,300 --> 00:14:01,594
Nothing I can't dodge.

235
00:14:04,060 --> 00:14:05,897
Can't you make those bullets hit me?

236
00:14:05,980 --> 00:14:06,810
Ah!

237
00:14:20,660 --> 00:14:22,140
Come on, knowledge boy!

238
00:14:24,960 --> 00:14:25,790
Compassion?

239
00:14:25,873 --> 00:14:27,000
In the heat of battle?

240
00:14:34,820 --> 00:14:36,780
This is a gross disappointment.

241
00:14:41,240 --> 00:14:42,760
I can't believe it.

242
00:14:42,940 --> 00:14:44,100
Vash the stampede.

243
00:14:44,200 --> 00:14:45,729
Is this all you amount to?

244
00:14:46,980 --> 00:14:49,040
I see absolutely nothing!

245
00:14:50,120 --> 00:14:50,960
Tell me!

246
00:14:51,220 --> 00:14:52,808
At least give me an answer!

247
00:14:52,920 --> 00:14:55,417
Tell me what you're seeing
right now at this moment!

248
00:14:55,500 --> 00:14:56,330
Tell me!

249
00:14:58,000 --> 00:15:01,560
Do you intend to die, Vash the Stampede?

250
00:15:03,500 --> 00:15:06,080
The time has come for you to use it.

251
00:15:09,540 --> 00:15:11,780
Go ahead, use it.

252
00:15:12,600 --> 00:15:13,700
Use it!

253
00:15:15,760 --> 00:15:17,880
There's something only you can do.

254
00:15:19,340 --> 00:15:20,660
Use it! Quickly!

255
00:15:24,440 --> 00:15:25,270
Stop it!

256
00:15:25,353 --> 00:15:26,183
Stop!

257
00:15:26,266 --> 00:15:27,096
Coward.

258
00:15:27,179 --> 00:15:29,328
I cannot believe he is
begging for his life.

259
00:15:32,120 --> 00:15:33,420
What is that?

260
00:15:39,080 --> 00:15:40,020
Don't do that!

261
00:15:48,960 --> 00:15:50,180
Not... the light!

